{
 "id": "BP-MASTER-15",
 "bp_entry": "BP-MASTER-15",
 "title": "Master data import: the storekeeper is refused and the JSON limits hold",
 "description": "The storekeeper (STOREKEEPER holds the import permission for opening lines only, not the wide one) sends the generic import of a catalog item, a place, an org unit and a code tag: each is refused 403 with nothing read (s1 to s4). The tenant administrator then sends an import of 201 empty records: the whole request is refused 413 before any record is looked at (the cap is 200, never a silent cut to 200); an import with an unknown schema version is refused 422 naming the version; a records field that is not a list is refused 422. Each refusal happens before any row is written, so the file has no cleanup. NOT covered here (runner gap, see the entry BP-MASTER-15): the spreadsheet and CSV limits (unreadable or oversized xlsx, header that is not a field, malformed CSV) need a request whose body is a binary or CSV file, a step kind the runner does not have. Needs modules catalog_items, locations, org and codes installed.",
 "tenant": "${tenant}",
 "inputs": [],
